@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@firebaseIdToken = paste-firebase-id-token
@plantId = paste-plant-id
@deviceToken = paste-device-token
@claimCode = paste-claim-code

# Protected user endpoints require a Firebase ID Token. Legacy password auth
# endpoints are disabled and return 410 Gone without issuing tokens.
# FIREBASE_AUTO_PROVISION_USERS defaults to true because the project has no
# pre-existing users. The first valid Firebase token creates an internal user.
# Oversized bodies return 413/PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE. Readiness, user API and device
# telemetry limits return 429/RATE_LIMITED with Retry-After. Defaults are listed
# in .env.example; production ingress must enforce equivalent per-client limits.
# Concurrent readiness probes share one DB check for the bounded
# READINESS_CACHE_TTL_MILLISECONDS window (default 1000 ms, maximum 5000 ms).
# Authenticated device uploads additionally share a PostgreSQL-backed per-device
# measurement quota; quota rejection writes no measurements.
# Measurements are hash-partitioned by device. The retention worker removes rows
# older than TELEMETRY_RETENTION_DAYS in bounded batches while preserving each
# device_latest_state row; history outside the retention window is unavailable.
# Production rejects requests that are not direct HTTPS and do not carry the
# trusted ingress value X-Forwarded-Proto: https with 426/HTTPS_REQUIRED. The
# header is accepted only when the direct peer is inside TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS;
# X-Forwarded-For is never trusted for this decision.
# Production server startup does not run Flyway and rejects MIGRATION_DATABASE_*
# secrets; apply migrations with the dedicated deployment job before rollout.
# Production also requires DEPLOYMENT_COMMIT_SHA; /health/live returns the exact
# value in X-Deployment-Commit for rollout and staging DAST correlation.
# SSE streams close at Firebase token expiry or the configured maximum lifetime,
# and also close if periodic ownership checks fail. Reconnect with a fresh token.
# API strings are checked before persistence: imageUrl must be credential-free
# HTTPS, claimCode is 32 lowercase hex characters, firmwareVersion is at most 100
# characters, and alert-rules accepts at most four unique public alert types.
# Claim, token rotation, calibration, alert-rule/acknowledgement changes and
# authentication/rate-limit rejections emit SECURITY_AUDIT without credentials,
# Firebase identifiers, email or request bodies; requestId provides correlation.
# The operator provisioning task no longer prints deviceToken/claimCode: it
# requires PROVISIONING_CONFIRM and writes them to DEVICE_CREDENTIALS_FILE (0600).
# User/device API responses, including errors, carry Cache-Control: no-store,
# Pragma: no-cache, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff and Referrer-Policy: no-referrer.

### Liveness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Disabled legacy register (410 Gone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register

### Disabled legacy login (410 Gone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login

### Disabled legacy refresh (410 Gone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

### Disabled legacy logout (410 Gone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout

### Current internal user profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### Permanently delete current account (destructive and idempotent)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### Create plant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plants
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Monstera","species":"Monstera deliciosa"}

### Claim provisioned device
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/claim
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"claimCode":"{{claimCode}}","plantId":"{{plantId}}"}

### Manually restore an owned device from temporary anomaly quarantine
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/devices/{{deviceId}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### Upload telemetry (device identity comes only from the token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/device/v1/measurements
Authorization: Device {{deviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"sequence":1,"firmwareVersion":"1.0.0","soilMoistureRaw":1530,"airTemperatureCelsius":23.5,"airHumidityPercent":51.0,"lightRaw":840}

### Latest plant state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plants/{{plantId}}/latest
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### Hourly history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plants/{{plantId}}/history?interval=1h
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}

### Live telemetry stream (SSE; reconnect with a fresh token after closure)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plants/{{plantId}}/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Accept: text/event-stream

### Alert rules
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/plants/{{plantId}}/alert-rules
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"rules":[{"type":"LOW_SOIL_MOISTURE","threshold":25.0,"requiredDurationSeconds":300,"recoveryDurationSeconds":300,"enabled":true}]}
